":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":607.8224391493999,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":54.0,"r":286.90739999999994,"t":710.2850999999999},"charspan":[0,418],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/1","text":"built classrooms and other education-related structures and ran awareness-raising programs on the importance of education.  (95-97) Burkina Faso continued to take part in the WFP Country Program (2011-2015) that promotes primary education and food security.(98) It also participated in a UNICEF-funded program to provide schooling to 5,000 child refugees in efforts to prevent the exploitation of refugee children.(99)"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"Burkina Faso","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":742.7102730030333,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":421.6313,"r":570.8972999999999,"t":764.664},"charspan":[0,12],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"Burkina Faso"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The Government of Burkina Faso has implemented or participated in social programs to address the worst forms of child labor in the production of cotton and in mining and quarrying, improving access to education and social services. However, research found no evidence that it has carried out programs to address the worst forms of child labor found in livestock raising, domestic service, forced begging, or street work .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":607.8224391493995,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":315.0036,"r":547.9981200000002,"t":710.2850999999996},"charspan":[0,421],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"The Government of Burkina Faso has implemented or participated in social programs to address the worst forms of child labor in the production of cotton and in mining and quarrying, improving access to education and social services. However, research found no evidence that it has carried out programs to address the worst forms of child labor found in livestock raising, domestic service, forced begging, or street work ."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"Based on the reporting above, the following actions would advance the elimination of the worst forms of child labor in Burkina Faso:","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":563.8953235591506,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":54.0,"r":533.1712499999998,"t":589.4499999999999},"charspan":[0,132],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"Based on the reporting above, the following actions would advance the elimination of the worst forms of child labor in Burkina Faso:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"REFERENCES","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":174.8117329625885,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":54.0809,"r":101.49830000000004,"t":182.41110000000003},"charspan":[0,10],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"REFERENCES"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"1.","orig":"1. UNESCO Institute for Statistics. Gross intake ratio to the last grade of primary. Total. ; accessed February 4, 2013; http://www.uis.unesco.org/Pages/default. aspx?SPSLanguage=EN. Data provided is the gross intake ratio to the last grade of primary school. This measure is a proxy measure for primary completion. For more information, please see the 'Children's Work and Education Statistics: Sources and Definitions' section of this report.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":107.70680119956387,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":54.0,"r":291.40560000000016,"t":163.02510000000007},"charspan":[0,444],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"UNESCO Institute for Statistics. Gross intake ratio to the last grade of primary. Total. ; accessed February 4, 2013; http://www.uis.unesco.org/Pages/default. aspx?SPSLanguage=EN. Data provided is the gross intake ratio to the last grade of primary school. This measure is a proxy measure for primary completion. For more information, please see the 'Children's Work and Education Statistics: Sources and Definitions' section of this report."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"2.","orig":"2. UCW. Analysis of Child Economic Activity and School Attendance Statistics from National Household or Child Labor Surveys . February 5, 2013. Reliable statistical data on the worst forms of child labor are especially difficult to collect given the often hidden or illegal nature of the worst forms. As a result, statistics on children's work in general are reported in this chart, which may or may not include the","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":58.266801199563815,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":54.00000000000001,"r":298.78488000000004,"t":103.9851000000001},"charspan":[0,415],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"UCW. Analysis of Child Economic Activity and School Attendance Statistics from National Household or Child Labor Surveys . February 5, 2013. Reliable statistical data on the worst forms of child labor are especially difficult to collect given the often hidden or illegal nature of the worst forms. As a result, statistics on children's work in general are reported in this chart, which may or may not include the"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":false,"label":"list_item","marker":"","orig":"worst forms of child labor.  For more information on sources used, the definition of working children and other indicators used in this report, please see the 'Children's Work and Education Statistics: Sources and Definitions' section of this report.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":147.68280119956387,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":328.9968,"r":555.2560799999997,"t":183.80110000000002},"charspan":[0,250],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"worst forms of child labor.  For more information on sources used, the definition of working children and other indicat